<section class="contact-methods">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>What to Send</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">
      A short email beats a form. The more of this you include, the more useful the first reply is.
    </p>

    <ul class="contact-list">
      <li>
        <span class="contact-label">Platform</span>
        Shopify, BigCommerce, WooCommerce, custom, headless &mdash; and roughly how long you&rsquo;ve been on it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="contact-label">Scale</span>
        Ballpark monthly revenue and order volume, plus how big the catalog is. Ranges are fine.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="contact-label">The problem</span>
        The one thing that&rsquo;s been stuck the longest &mdash; conversion, operations, reporting, or a platform decision you keep deferring.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="contact-label">Who&rsquo;s involved</span>
        Whether you have developers, an agency, or a freelancer today, and what they currently own.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="contact-label">Email</span>
        <a href="mailto:hello@infiniteframeworks.com">hello@infiniteframeworks.com</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="contact-label">Location</span>
        Based in North Carolina, working with stores anywhere in the US.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="contact-reassurance">
      No mailing list, no automated sequence, no discovery call before you know whether there&rsquo;s
      anything to discuss.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

